{title: Jesus, the Very Thought of Thee}
{artist: Bernard of Clairvaux, tr. Edward Caswall / John B. Dykes}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 125}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 445. First appeared in the Hymnal for Use in the English Church, by J)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Je[G]sus, the [Am]very thought [D]of [G]Thee
[D7]With [G]sweetness fills the [D]breast;
[Am]But sweeter far [A7]Thy [D]face to see,
[G]And [C]in Thy [G]pre__[D7]__sence [G]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]O [G]hope of [Am]every con[D]trite [G]heart,
[D7]O [G]joy of all the [D]meek,
[Am]To those who fall, [A7]how [D]kind Thou art!
[G]How [C]good to [G]those__[D7]__ who [G]seek!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Em]But [G]what to [Am]those who find? [D]Ah, [G]this
[D7]Nor [G]tongue nor pen can [D]show;
[Am]The love of Je[A7]sus, [D]what it is,
[G]None [C]but His [G]loved__[D7]__ ones [G]know.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Em]O [G]Jesus, [Am]King most won[D]der[G]ful
[D7]Thou [G]Conqueror re[D]nowned,
[Am]Thou sweetness most [A7]in[D]effable
[G]In [C]whom all [G]joys__[D7]__ are [G]found!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[Em]When [G]once Thou [Am]visitest [D]the [G]heart,
[D7]Then [G]truth begins to [D]shine,
[Am]Then earthly va[A7]ni[D]ties depart,
[G]Then [C]kindles [G]love__[D7]__ di[G]vine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[Em]O [G]Jesus, [Am]light of all [D]be[G]low,
[D7]Thou [G]fount of living [D]fire,
[Am]Surpassing all [A7]the [D]joys we know,
[G]And [C]all we [G]can__[D7]__ de[G]sire.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
[Em]Je[G]sus, may [Am]all confess [D]Thy [G]name,
[D7]Thy [G]wondrous love ad[D]ore,
[Am]And, seeking Thee, [A7]them[D]selves inflame
[G]To [C]seek Thee [G]more__[D7]__ and [G]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
[Em]Thee, [G]Jesus, [Am]may our voic[D]es [G]bless,
[D7]Thee [G]may we love a[D]lone,
[Am]And ever in [A7]our [D]lives express
[G]The [C]image [G]of__[D7]__ Thine [G]own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
[Em]O [G]Jesus, [Am]Thou the beau[D]ty [G]art
[D7]Of [G]angel worlds a[D]bove;
[Am]Thy name is mu[A7]sic [D]to the heart,
[G]In[C]flaming [G]it__[D7]__ with [G]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 12}
[Em]Ce[G]lestial [Am]sweetness un[D]al[G]loyed,
[D7]Who [G]eat Thee hunger [D]still;
[Am]Who drink of Thee [A7]still [D]feel a void
[G]Which [C]only [G]Thou__[D7]__ canst [G]fill.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 14}
[Em]A[G]bide with [Am]us, and let [D]Thy [G]light
[D7]Shine, [G]Lord, on every [D]heart;
[Am]Dispel the dark[A7]ness [D]of our night;
[G]And [C]joy to [G]all__[D7]__ im[G]part.
{end_of_verse}
